  <data name="Faq_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Frequently asked questions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_MetaDescription" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Age to drive a scooter, charging, park transport, rain, cancellation, strollers and wagons, and what to bring.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How old do I have to be to drive a mobility scooter?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The driver must be 18 or older. A younger passenger can ride along only on a model that allows a second rider.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How do I charge the scooter?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Charge it overnight in your room with the charger we leave with you. A full night covers a full park day. Take the key out whenever you park it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Does the equipment fit on the park transport?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Disney buses and the Skyliner take equipment up to 30 by 48 inches, and every model at or under that size carries the badge on its page. Strollers must stay under 31 by 52 inches inside the Disney parks.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What happens if it rains?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Rain does not stop the rental. Park the equipment under cover during a storm and dry the seat before using it again. A rain cover is available for strollers.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can I cancel?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A5" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Yes. The terms page carries the cancellation window in force.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can I bring a wagon into the parks instead?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A6" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No. Wagons are not allowed inside the Disney parks, which is why we rent strollers and not wagons.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What should I bring?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A7" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nothing. The equipment arrives clean, tested and charged, with everything it needs.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_Q8" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How do I reach you during the trip?</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Faq_A8" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>By phone or WhatsApp, on the number on the contact page, during the hours listed there.</value>
  </data>
